{#
mail/_jobs_indicator.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Background work, in the topbar, and only when there is any.

A whole-view action — "mark all 5,455 read" — runs on a worker now, so the page
answers immediately and the work happens somewhere the user cannot see. This is
where they can see it.

NOT RENDERED WHEN THERE IS NOTHING TO SAY, and that is the whole design of it.
An indicator that is always present is another permanent fixture to learn to
ignore; one that appears only while something is happening is read the moment it
appears. The frame collapses to nothing when the list is empty.

A job that SUCCEEDED does not linger — see BackgroundJobRepository::findVisibleForUser.
It has already changed the list the user is looking at, so an indicator
reporting it says something they can see, and an indicator that appears and
disappears on its own is a topbar that reflows for no reason. A FAILURE is the
opposite: nothing changed, and if this does not say so, nothing does.

Refreshed by core--mercure on `jobs.changed`, which carries no state: the row is
the record and a missed nudge costs one stale render, never a wrong answer.
#}
{# NO `src`, deliberately. A frame with one fetches itself on every page load,
   which is a request per page for every user answering "nothing is happening"
   almost every time — and it broke the appearance preview's assertion that it
   loads no mail, which was right to complain.

   The topbar renders this with whatever jobs exist, which is one indexed query
   it is already making a page render for. From then on it is replaced: by the
   response to starting a job, and by mail--jobs when Mercure says one moved.
   The route stays, because that is what mail--jobs re-reads. #}
<turbo-frame id="jobs-indicator">
    {% if jobs is defined and jobs|length > 0 %}
        {% set active = jobs|filter(j => j.isActive())|length %}
        {% set failed = jobs|filter(j => j.state.value == 'failed')|length %}

        <div class="relative" data-controller="ui--dropdown">
            <button
                type="button"
                data-action="click->ui--dropdown#toggle"
                class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-center w-9 h-9 rounded-lg
                       text-ink-muted hover:bg-hover transition-colors flex-shrink-0"
                aria-label="{{ 'jobs.heading'|trans }}"
                title="{{ 'jobs.heading'|trans }}"
            >
                {# Spinning only while something is actually running: a static
                   glyph for "finished, here is what happened" and a moving one
                   for "still going" is the difference the eye reads first. #}
                <i class="fa-solid fa-list-check text-base {{ active > 0 ? 'fa-fade' : '' }}
                          {{ failed > 0 ? 'text-danger' : (active > 0 ? 'text-accent' : '') }}"
                   aria-hidden="true"></i>
            </button>

            <div
                data-ui--dropdown-target="menu"
                data-enter="slide-down"
                class="hidden absolute right-0 top-full mt-1 z-30 w-80
                       rounded-pane bg-pane-soft backdrop-blur-sm
                       border border-line shadow-pop p-2 text-sm"
            >
                <p class="px-2 py-1 text-xs font-semibold text-ink">{{ 'jobs.heading'|trans }}</p>

                <ul class="mt-1 space-y-1">
                    {% for job in jobs %}
                        <li class="rounded-lg px-2 py-2 {{ job.isActive() ? 'bg-accent-soft/40' : '' }}">
                            <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-2">
                                <span class="text-xs font-medium text-ink truncate">
                                    {{ job.kind.labelKey()|trans }}
                                </span>
                                <span class="text-[11px] text-ink-faint tabular-nums shrink-0">
                                    {% if job.state.value == 'failed' %}
                                        {{ 'jobs.state.failed'|trans }}
                                    {% elseif job.state.value == 'done' %}
                                        {{ 'jobs.state.done'|trans({ '%count%': job.total }) }}
                                    {% elseif job.total > 0 %}
                                        {{ job.processed }} / {{ job.total }}
                                    {% else %}
                                        {{ 'jobs.state.queued'|trans }}
                                    {% endif %}
                                </span>
                            </div>

                            {% if job.isActive() and job.total > 0 %}
                                {# Width from the job's own percent(), which
                                   floors and never reports more than 100 — a
                                   bar that reaches the end before the work does
                                   is worse than no bar. #}
                                <div class="mt-1.5 h-1 rounded-full bg-line overflow-hidden">
                                    <div class="h-full bg-accent transition-all duration-300"
                                         style="width: {{ job.percent() }}%"></div>
                                </div>
                            {% endif %}

                            {% if job.failureReason %}
                                <p class="mt-1 text-[11px] text-danger break-words">{{ job.failureReason }}</p>
                            {% endif %}
                        </li>
                    {% endfor %}
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    {% endif %}
</turbo-frame>
